# Token-saving rules

## Reading files
- Never open `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `package-lock.json`, or binary/image files in `public/`.
- Search (Grep/Glob) before reading. Read only the relevant line range of a file, not the whole file, when it is long.
- Don't re-read a file already read in this conversation unless it may have changed.
- Rely on `project-context.mdc` for stack and layout instead of exploring the repo.
- Content/copy changes (text, links, projects, skills, experience) belong in `src/data/content.js` — go there first.

## Editing
- Make targeted edits (StrReplace) instead of rewriting whole files.
- Don't add new dependencies when an existing one (framer-motion, lucide-react, react-icons, Tailwind) covers the need.

## Replying
- Be concise. Skip preambles and recaps of what the user said.
- Show only changed snippets, never full unchanged files.
- Don't explain basic React/Tailwind concepts unless asked.
- Skip running builds or dev servers unless needed to verify a change.
